nt is  protecting young people and I've always  thought protecting young people I'm a  parent myself and I find it completely  so  destroying to understand that there's so  many young people that have been abused  in this way and there's a responsible  parent responsible adults I'm doing  everything in my power to make sure that  this is adequately tackled here in South  Yorkshire and especially in Rotherham  we're just gonna hear if you can just  wait just a moment we're just gonna hear  from the report author Alexis J  something that she had to say yesterday  if all of the authorities involved  officers and members had been less  concerned with their own agendas and  prejudices and kept their focus on the  children's welfare some of these  children might not have suffered that  the abuse and brutality we read about  and heard about what's your response to  that well of course if professor J is  found areas of concern around actually  should have named the people involved I  gave an interview to Miss J as part of  this this review and I was very explicit  that where criticism should be made or  needed to be made it should be as open  and explicit as possible and you know if  that's the findings of Miss J then  that's from Miss J to speak to that but  clearly I wasn't aware or involved in  any inappropriate behavior in that sense  so in a sense the report perhaps could  have gone a little further in  identifying those particularly  responsible because generalizing and  making general statements is obviously  very difficult for the people in  positions to take action to actually  take that appropriate action and you  gave evidence didn't you to the Home  Affairs Select Committee on this issue  in that you said whilst I was aware that  some of the vulnerable young people I  saw could have suffered sexual abuse I  was not informed of individual  circumstances I did not believe it would  have been appropriate for me to request  to meet victims of child sexual  exploitat